Implementing a multi-tree list (also known as a hierarchical tree view) in an Angular application involves several steps. Below is a high-level overview of how you can achieve this:

### Step 1: Set Up Your Project

First, ensure you have Node.js and npm installed on your system. Then create a new Angular project if you haven't already:

```bash
ng new my-multi-tree-list-app
cd my-multi-tree-list-app
```

### Step 2: Install Required Dependencies

Install the necessary dependencies for creating a multi-tree list.

```bash
npm install @angular/cdk @angular/material @types/node rxjs material-icons-icon font-awesome-skyicons
```

### Step 3: Create Tree Data Model

Define the structure of your data model. Each node will represent a folder or file in the hierarchy.

```typescript
// src/app/models/tree-node.model.ts
export class TreeNode {
    id: string;
    name: string;
    children?: TreeNode[];
}
```

### Step 4: Implement Multi-Tree List Component

Create a component where the multi-tree list will be displayed.

```typescript
// src/app/multi-tree-list.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { TreeNode } from './models/tree-node.model';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multi-tree-list',
  templateUrl: './multi-tree-list.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./multi-tree-list.component.css']
})
export class MultiTreeListComponent {
  nodes: TreeNode[] = [
    { id: '0', name: 'Root' },
    { id: '1', name: 'Child 1', children: [ { id: '1.1', name: 'Subchild 1' }, { id: '1.2', name: 'Subchild 2' } ] },
    // Add more nodes as needed
  ];

  expandAll(): void {
    this.nodes.forEach(node => {
      node.expanded = true;
    });
  }

  collapseAll(): void {
    this.nodes.forEach(node => {
      node.expanded = false;
    });
  }
}
```

### Step 5: Display the Multi-Tree List

In your template, use Angular Material's `mat-tree` component to display the multi-tree list.

```html
<!-- src/app/multi-tree-list.component.html -->
<mat-tree [nodes]="nodes" (nodeSelect)="onNodeSelect($event)">
  <mat-tree-node *ngFor="let node of nodes">
    {{ node.name }}
  </mat-tree-node>
</mat-tree>

<button mat-raised-button color="primary" (click)="expandAll()">Expand All</button>
<button mat-raised-button color="primary" (click)="collapseAll()">Collapse All</button>
```

### Step 6: Handle Node Selection

Add event listeners to handle selection changes.

```typescript
// src/app/multi-tree-list.component.ts
...
onNodeSelect(event: MatTreeNodeEvent): void {
  console.log('Node selected:', event.node);
}

...
```

### Step 7: Style the Multi-Tree List

Style the multi-tree list using CSS.

```css
/* src/app/multi-tree-list.component.css */
.mat-tree ul {
  padding-left: 0;
}

.mat-tree-node:hover,
.mat-tree-node.selected {
  background-color: #f8f9fa !important;
}

.mat-tree-node {
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

### Step 8: Run Your Application

Finally, run your application to see the multi-tree list in action.

```bash
ng serve
```

